{
  "feature": "Spare requests close-out (plan 2026-10-22-spare-requests.md; handoff design_handoff_the99_spare_requests): Shopping's marks and key (3b), the friends-with-a-spare modal's four answers (3b), the cart's By friend view (3c), /friends' Waiting on you and Your requests, Home's lead story and Settings' feed kind (3d), and the friend-spares About entry with requests on (PR 4)",
  "note": "Needs SOCIAL_FRIENDS_ENABLED, SPARE_REQUESTS_ENABLED, HOME_FEED_ENABLED, ALL_DECKS_CART_ENABLED, SWAP_TOOLS_ENABLED, COLLECTION_EDIT_ENABLED and COMMANDERS_PLACE_ENABLED on for the reader (the last puts Friends and its badge in the tab bar and rail, as the boards draw them) (MOMENTS_ENABLED off, so no bubble covers a press). FIXTURES ON A SCRATCH BRANCH OFF local-dev ONLY: they are social, collection and spare-request rows. The reader (the audit account) needs: one deck SPARE_DECK whose Shopping list holds six unowned cards; five friends sharing spares through two pods (`Thursday pod`, `Cube night`); the reader's asks in every state Your requests draws, for those cards: SPARE_REQUESTED open to one friend while a second friend also has a spare (Requested, and Ask instead on the other), SPARE_ACCEPTED answered yes, SPARE_DECLINED answered no while another friend still has a spare, SPARE_EXPIRED unanswered past 14 days with the holder still offering (Ask again), SPARE_ASK held by a friend and never asked (Ask), one open ask whose holder then stopped sharing (No longer spare) and one for a card on none of the reader's decks (No longer needed); two friends' open asks for the reader's own spares, one naming the asker's deck (Waiting on you, Home's lead). Every visit moves `user_prefs.feed_seen_at` (Home) and `friends_seen_at` (/friends), so the second width would photograph no lead story and no unseen mark: hold both at the seeded values for the run. The rows write nothing; Yes and No receipts are pressed in a separate run because a press answers the ask for every later cell. The About row draws the PR 4 caption (Press “Ask” beside a friend...), so photograph it from a server running the close-out branch.",
